From 21428a574cb56cc0cc760cc476328d3ac88f7ff1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaejinaa <wowls7990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:24:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(gitlab): clone and push through the proxy

The proxy takes the upstream host, the credential and the fast-forward check from the connection's connector: GitHub keeps its constants, githubToken and compare API byte for byte; GitLab uses the instance's base URL, HTTP Basic for git, PRIVATE-TOKEN for REST and its merge-base API. Scopes are derived per connector, and the computer sync picks the GitLab connection when no GitHub one is connected, handing it the same agtgit1 credential and never a GitLab token. git_clone is the one git tool offered on a GitLab connection; pull requests, branch deletion and branch approvals stay GitHub-only.
